Modified by the RevolaOS authors since 2026-11-08.
RepriseOS's history at the fork point is archived in
https://github.com/paviro/revola-repriseos-heritage.

Files that carry an "Adapted from" or copyright header keep that header.

The release bundle also carries the extensions, games, apps and USB helper
built from their repositories, with the eApp SDK runtime (adapted from the
RepriseOS game SDK) linked into the games and apps. Third-party work in this
repository and the bundle, summarised from those repositories' NOTICE files:

- Rockbox (https://github.com/Rockbox/rockbox): the bootloader, dual-boot
  installer and hardware drivers, built from source at the commit in
  boot/dependencies.lock; the panic screen's I2C sequence; the flash markers
  of the disk check; the USB helper; the crossfeed filters, channel modes and
  compressor of the extensions; the 2048 game with its tile artwork by Franklin
  Wei and the high score table by Linus Nielsen Feltzing; the Dice app by
  Brandon Low. GPL-2.0-or-later.
- Cupertino Icons (https://github.com/flutter/packages): the Settings glyphs
  and the Appearance extension's glyphs. MIT, see
  core/assets/LICENSE.cupertino-icons.
- The Classic theme's dark background, carried by the Appearance extension, is
  RepriseOS's themes/dark/background-dark-image.png by lgreitis (5ec8799). Its
  dark palette comes from RepriseOS's payload/dark_mode.c (01c89f6) by lgreitis
  and Alex Ball (alexballvideos-netizen). GPL-3.0-only.
- Khronos OpenGL ES 1.1 and KHR platform headers
  (https://github.com/KhronosGroup/OpenGL-Registry,
  https://github.com/KhronosGroup/EGL-Registry): the GL headers of the eApp
  SDK, compiled into the games and apps. MIT and Apache-2.0.
- giek2000 (https://github.com/giek2000/ipod-classic-firmware-research): iPod
  firmware research.

Each release publishes the source of everything in the bundle alongside it.

No Apple firmware ships in this repository or its builds. Building reads the
firmware from an IPSW the user supplies.
